    "termsOfUse": "Users interested in the use of DuST for research purposes may obtain the dataset in the publicly distributable format and in the full text format. Users can freely download the publicly distributable format from the GitHub repository (<a href=\"https://github.com/projecte-aina/dynamic-stance-analysis\">https://github.com/projecte-aina/dynamic-stance-analysis</a>). Researchers affiliated with universities or not-for-profit research institutes may use the full version of DuST in accordance with the Data Transfer Agreement provided by the University of Groningen. The data may be used only for the purpose of conducting not-for-profit scientific research. It is not allowed to actively search online for any of the information contained in the full version of DuST. It is not allowed to disclose the full version of DuST to any third party or otherwise use it for your own benefit or for the benefit of a third party, without first obtaining written consent from the University of Groningen.",
    "restrictions": "Signing of a Data Transfer Agreement provided by the University of Groningen is part of the procedure for re-use of the full version of DuST. The agreement will enter into force as of the date both parties have signed it. The agreement will continue to be effective during the period that you possess the data. During that period, you cannot terminate the agreement. The University of Groningen may terminate the agreement if you have not cured a breach of the agreement within a reasonable period of being notified of such a breach. At the request of the University of Groningen, you will return or destroy all copies of the full version of DuST.",
    "termsOfAccess": "Permission for re-use can be granted by the University of Groningen Digital Competence Centre on behalf of the first author after inspecting credentials and the reason for request. The procedure starts with a request for access via this dataset at DataverseNL. Signing of a Data Transfer Agreement is part of the procedure for re-use of the data.",
